:"Architecture","stem":"Which feature occupies much of the upper level of Villa Savoye beside its enclosed rooms?","choices":["A pitched-roof attic","A roof garden","A two-storey ballroom","An enclosed winter garden","A barrel-vaulted studio"],"answer":"A roof garden","correctIndex":1,"explanation":"The roof garden is part of Le Corbusier's programme at Villa Savoye and one of his Five Points.","group":"Architecture and society","topic74":"Architecture and society","format":"context_relation","skill74":"context_relation","task101":"context","examLanguages":["en","it"],"scope":"shared","editorialStatus74":"ready","reviewStatus":"editorially_reviewed","publication_ready":true,"previewOnly95":false,"version":"editorial-v101","difficulty74":"unrated","references":[],"evidenceStatus101":"editorial factual review; individual external verification not claimed","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0432","relatedNodeIds":["FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0432"],"fingerprint":"b48ce783cc58b010e7dd","semanticKey101":"f127a1dd072be2255c9bfd41eb51eec7e05a4ae66d53c906f32fd96171517bda","workNames101":[],"editorialRevision101":"specific factual/distractor/duplicate correction","practiceRepetitionKeys95":["FACT:ARCHED-NEW101-0432","WORK:villa savoye"],"testedRelation95":"v101:8ac3b13c3f7ac8d1d456","imageId":null,"semanticReview101":"Replaced duplicate or reverse restatement with a distinct factual relation.","distractorReview101":"Same semantic category; obvious unrelated choices replaced."},{"id":"ARCHED-NEW101-0433","qid":1010433,"major":"Architecture","stem":"The Barcelona Pavilion's walls chiefly demonstrate which idea?","choices":["A centralised radial plan","A sequence of closed axial rooms","A rigid nave-and-aisles hierarchy","Space shaped by independent planes","A symmetrical courtyard enclosure"],"answer":"Space shaped by independent planes","correctIndex":3,"explanation":"Its freestanding wall planes articulate space without forming a conventional cellular load-bearing plan.","group":"Ar