 d'Habitation, internal streets principally provide access to:","choices":["Single-level hotel suites","Interlocking apartments","Split-level exhibition galleries","Separate office floors","Detached studio units"],"answer":"Interlocking apartments","correctIndex":1,"explanation":"The internal corridors serve apartments arranged within a large collective-housing structure.","group":"Architecture and society","topic74":"Architecture and society","format":"context_relation","skill74":"context_relation","task101":"context_relation","examLanguages":["en","it"],"scope":"shared","editorialStatus74":"ready","reviewStatus":"editorially_reviewed","publication_ready":true,"previewOnly95":false,"version":"editorial-v101","difficulty74":"unrated","references":[],"evidenceStatus101":"editorial factual review; individual external verification not claimed","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0436","relatedNodeIds":["FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0436"],"fingerprint":"f4d2cfe04de87aea6982","semanticKey101":"e752e19dd8e04ccf4302086660214340a3d0f08bd1cf307741f7b94dc7986910","workNames101":["Unité d'Habitation"],"editorialRevision101":"specific factual/distractor/duplicate correction","practiceRepetitionKeys95":["FACT:ARCHED-NEW101-0436","WORK:unite d habitation"],"testedRelation95":"v101:a1f4243bbf0911491f95","distractorReview101":"Same semantic category; obvious unrelated choices replaced."},{"id":"ARCHED-NEW101-0437","qid":1010437,"major":"Architecture","stem":"Which building combines a convent programme with individual cells and communal religious spaces?","choices":["Sainte-Marie de La Tourette","Notre-Dame du Haut","Church of the Autostrada","Church of the Light","Sainte-Bernadette du Banlay"],"answer":"Sainte-Marie de La Tourette","correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Le Corbusier's La Tourette was designed for a Dominican community.","group":"Architecture and society","topic74":"Architecture and society","format":"context_relation","skill74":"context_relation","task101":"context_relation","examL