 slabs","Sandstone ashlar","Quartzite slabs","Travertine blocks","Basalt blocks"],"answer":"Quartzite slabs","correctIndex":2,"explanation":"Zumthor's stacked stone surfaces connect the bathing spaces to the Alpine geology.","group":"Architecture and society","topic74":"Architecture and society","format":"context_relation","skill74":"context_relation","task101":"context_relation","examLanguages":["en","it"],"scope":"shared","editorialStatus74":"ready","reviewStatus":"editorially_reviewed","publication_ready":true,"previewOnly95":false,"version":"editorial-v101","difficulty74":"unrated","references":[],"evidenceStatus101":"editorial factual review; individual external verification not claimed","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0447","relatedNodeIds":["FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0447"],"fingerprint":"260acd2d23945e31b6ee","semanticKey101":"d0d380379ef26ce8675c1ffbee19f4838d4fc452c0407d17d4b8d1875adc37cd","workNames101":["Therme Vals"],"editorialRevision101":"specific factual/distractor/duplicate correction","practiceRepetitionKeys95":["FACT:ARCHED-NEW101-0447","WORK:therme vals"],"testedRelation95":"v101:00a1b3f7a6e9b3318288","distractorReview101":"Same semantic category; obvious unrelated choices replaced."},{"id":"ARCHED-NEW101-0448","qid":1010448,"major":"Architecture","stem":"Kolumba in Cologne preserves a connection with the city's past by incorporating:","choices":["A ruined civic palace","A Roman bath complex","A former synagogue","A medieval city gate","The ruins of a church"],"answer":"The ruins of a church","correctIndex":4,"explanation":"Zumthor's museum integrates the surviving ruins of Saint Kolumba and an existing chapel.","group":"Architecture and society","topic74":"Architecture and society","format":"context_relation","skill74":"context_relation","task101":"context_relation","examLanguages":["en","it"],"scope":"shared","editorialStatus74":"ready","reviewStatus":"editorially_reviewed","publication_ready":true,"previewOnly95":false,"version":"editorial-v101","