ower supporting steps"],"answer":"It comprises the lower supporting steps","correctIndex":4,"explanation":"The stylobate is the upper platform bearing the columns; the stereobate refers to the supporting stepped substructure below.","group":"Architecture and society","topic74":"Architecture and society","format":"context_relation","skill74":"context_relation","task101":"context","examLanguages":["en","it"],"scope":"shared","editorialStatus74":"ready","reviewStatus":"editorially_reviewed","publication_ready":true,"previewOnly95":false,"version":"editorial-v101","difficulty74":"unrated","references":[],"evidenceStatus101":"editorial factual review; individual external verification not claimed","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0451","relatedNodeIds":["FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0451"],"fingerprint":"da32661156125a2c2770","semanticKey101":"70e43732faf2b0320b8e1e27c5463855c11a081e1264d9b593f6062ed5ff34b2","workNames101":[],"editorialRevision101":"specific factual/distractor/duplicate correction","practiceRepetitionKeys95":["FACT:ARCHED-NEW101-0451","WORK:nakagin capsule tower"],"testedRelation95":"v101:d8abde0469f33b3c1da4","imageId":null,"semanticReview101":"Replaced duplicate or reverse restatement with a distinct factual relation."},{"id":"ARCHED-NEW101-0452","qid":1010452,"major":"Architecture","stem":"The Montreal Biosphere demonstrates the structural principle of a:","choices":["Pneumatic membrane dome","Geodesic dome","Cable-net dome","Folded-plate roof","Lamella vault"],"answer":"Geodesic dome","correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Its spherical lattice distributes forces through a network of interconnected elements.","group":"Architecture and society","topic74":"Architecture and society","format":"context_relation","skill74":"context_relation","task101":"context_relation","examLanguages":["en","it"],"scope":"shared","editorialStatus74":"ready","reviewStatus":"editorially_reviewed","publication_ready":true,"previewOnly95":false,"version":"editorial-v101","difficulty74":"unra